questions.stem:
A stand builder draws rows of growing width, and a counter tallies every cell it visits. What does the printer output?
int visits = 0;
for (int i = 1; i <= 4; i++) {
    for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        visits++;
    }
}
System.out.println(visits);

A scanner skips one column of every row, and only the other columns count towards a total. What does the printer output?
int body = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < 3; r++) {
    for (int c = 0; c < 4; c++) {
        if (c == 2) continue;
        body++;
    }
}
System.out.println(body);

A four-by-four sweep stops each row as soon as the product of the two indexes reaches six, and the counter runs before the test. What does the printer output?
int scans = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < 4; r++) {
    for (int c = 0; c < 4; c++) {
        if (r * c == 6) break;
        scans++;
    }
}
System.out.println(scans);

A stress test's inner routine bumps the outer counter three times, and a tally records how many times the outer body finishes. What does the printer output?
int passes = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < 3; j++) {
        i++;
    }
    passes++;
}
System.out.println(passes);

A refill loop is allowed two refills and no more than five ticks of work, and it prints both counters when it stops. What does the printer output?
int i = 0;
int taken = 0;
while (i < 5 && taken < 2) {
    taken++;
    i++;
}
System.out.println(i + "," + taken);

A surcharge is seeded with a standing fee and no customer rows are present, so the loop body never runs once. What does the printer output?
int n = 0;
int total = 10;
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    total = total + 5;
}
System.out.println(total);

A note variable is only written on the even passes of a five-pass loop, and its value is read once the loop is done. What does the printer output?
int last = -1;
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    if (i % 2 == 0) {
        last = i;
    }
}
System.out.println(last);

A hunt leaves the counter declared outside the loop so it can be read afterwards, and it gives up on the value four. What does the printer output?
int i;
for (i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    if (i == 4) break;
}
System.out.println(i);

A ticket desk hands out one ticket per pass and takes two units of stock each time, starting from an odd seed. What does the printer output?
int stock = 7;
int tickets = 0;
while (stock > 0) {
    tickets++;
    stock = stock - 2;
}
System.out.println(tickets + " " + stock);

A report prints one total per row, and the author expected each row to start from a fresh total. What does the printer actually output?
int rowSum = 0;
for (int r = 1; r <= 3; r++) {
    for (int c = 1; c <= 3; c++) {
        rowSum = rowSum + c;
    }
    System.out.print(rowSum + " ");
}
System.out.println("end");

A billing pass adds a waiting time into the total only when the time is above zero, and two of the five rows are zero. What does the printer output?
int[] wait = {4, 0, 7, 0, 2};
int billed = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < wait.length; i++) {
    if (wait[i] > 0) {
        billed = billed + wait[i];
    }
}
System.out.println(billed);

A print job keeps going while the printed count is under twenty, adding seven each pass, and the page counter starts at one. What does the printer output?
int page = 1;
int printed = 0;
while (printed < 20) {
    printed = printed + 7;
    page++;
}
System.out.println(page + " " + printed);

A scan visits three rows of two cells and keeps the best score together with the row that held it, using a strict improvement test. What does the printer output?
int winner = -1;
int best = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < 3; r++) {
    for (int c = 0; c < 2; c++) {
        int score = r * 10 + c;
        if (score > best) {
            best = score;
            winner = r;
        }
    }
}
System.out.println(winner + " " + best);

A running total adds the odd positions and subtracts the even ones across six passes of a counter. What does the printer output?
int n = 6;
int sum = 0;
for (int k = 1; k <= n; k++) {
    if (k % 2 == 1) {
        sum = sum + k;
    } else {
        sum = sum - k;
    }
}
System.out.println(sum);

A trend check keeps the previous value in a variable that starts at zero, and counts every pass where the new value is strictly larger. What does the printer output?
int prev = 0;
int seen = 0;
int steps = 0;
for (int k = 0; k < 4; k++) {
    int cur = k * 2;
    if (cur > prev) {
        seen++;
    }
    prev = cur;
    steps++;
}
System.out.println(seen + " " + steps);

A packing routine counts the cells of each row and then multiplies the running figure at the end of every row. What does the printer output?
int both = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < 2; r++) {
    for (int c = 0; c < 3; c++) {
        both++;
    }
    both = both * 2;
}
System.out.println(both);

A scorer compares two row totals built from a flat array and keeps the largest one it has seen, using a strict test. What does the printer output?
int[] rowScores = {2, 3, 1, 4};
int bestRow = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < 2; r++) {
    int rowSum = 0;
    for (int c = 0; c < 2; c++) {
        rowSum = rowSum + rowScores[r * 2 + c];
    }
    if (rowSum > bestRow) {
        bestRow = rowSum;
    }
}
System.out.println(bestRow);

A pyramid is filled from the widest row down to the narrowest, and the author wants every row to be as wide as its number. What does the printer output?
int rows = 4;
int cells = 0;
for (int r = rows; r > 0; r--) {
    for (int c = 0; c < r; c++) {
        cells++;
    }
}
System.out.println(cells);

A fuel loop keeps flying while there would be fuel left after the next leg, and each leg consumes a fixed amount. What does the printer output?
int fuel = 10;
int legs = 0;
int used = 3;
while (fuel - used > 0) {
    fuel = fuel - used;
    legs++;
}
System.out.println(legs + " " + fuel);

A drain loop lowers its own ceiling on the passes where the counter is odd, and the continue on the even passes still returns to the guard. What does the printer output?
int n = 4;
int i = 0;
while (i < n) {
    i++;
    if (i % 2 == 0) continue;
    n--;
}
System.out.println(i + " " + n);

A sweep tests every position of a four by four board and counts those whose two indexes add to three. What does the printer output?
int hits = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < 4; j++) {
        if (i + j == 3) {
            hits++;
        }
    }
}
System.out.println(hits);

A formatter reads the width of each row from an array, so the shape it produces has rows of three different lengths. What does the printer output?
int[] limits = {2, 3, 1};
int total = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < limits.length; r++) {
    for (int c = 0; c < limits[r]; c++) {
        total = total + 1;
    }
}
System.out.println(total);

A two-ended pointer walks in from both sides of a list and records the pair it holds after each step. What does the printer output?
int steps = 0;
String trail = "";
for (int i = 0, j = 6; i < j; i++, j--) {
    steps++;
    trail = trail + i + "-" + j + " ";
}
System.out.println(trail + "| " + steps);

A load check sets a flag when it meets a busy reading and counts the readings it walked through, and nothing ever clears the flag. What does the printer output?
int[] load = {3, 8, 2, 9};
boolean sawBusy = false;
int count = 0;
for (int v : load) {
    if (v > 5) {
        sawBusy = true;
    }
    count++;
}
System.out.println(sawBusy + " " + count);

A builder measures each row in a growing triangle and copies the size it found into one variable that is printed after the loop. What does the printer output?
int row = 0;
for (int r = 1; r <= 4; r++) {
    int filled = 0;
    for (int c = 1; c <= r; c++) {
        filled++;
    }
    row = filled;
}
System.out.println(row);

An outer loop runs four times and counts its own passes, while the inner loop has a range that can never contain a value. What does the printer output?
int passes = 0;
int cells = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < 4; r++) {
    passes++;
    for (int c = 0; c < 0; c++) {
        cells++;
    }
}
System.out.println(passes + " " + cells);

A billing loop advances its counter at the end of the body on the passes that charge, and the even passes step first and then continue. What does the printer output?
int i = 0;
int paid = 0;
while (i < 6) {
    if (i % 2 == 0) {
        i++;
        continue;
    }
    i = i + 1;
    paid++;
}
System.out.println(i + " " + paid);

A running total is printed from inside the loop on every pass, so the printer shows the value as it stands each time. What does the printer output?
int sum = 0;
for (int k = 1; k <= 4; k++) {
    sum = sum + k;
    System.out.print(sum + " ");
}
System.out.println("end");

A pairing sweep walks three rows against four columns and counts only the pairs whose two indexes differ. What does the printer output?
int pairs = 0;
for (int a = 0; a < 3; a++) {
    for (int b = 0; b < 4; b++) {
        if (a != b) {
            pairs++;
        }
    }
}
System.out.println(pairs);

A banner widens itself as it goes, and the inner loop takes its width from a value the outer body has just increased. What does the printer output?
int width = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < 4; r++) {
    width = width + 1;
    for (int c = 0; c < width; c++) {
        System.out.print("*");
    }
    System.out.print("|");
}
System.out.println("end");
